    "title": "Beyond the Headlines: FDA Warning Letters to GLP-1 Compounders - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Beth Siemer ,\n19 days ago As part of a larger crackdown on direct-to-consumer prescription drug advertising, the FDA published over 55 warning letters on September 16 to online sellers of compounded versions of the popular GLP-1 medications for type-2 diabetes and weight loss. The letters alleged that some of the words used in advertising the products gave rise to an “Unlawful Sale of Unapproved and Misbranded Drugs to United States Consumers over the Internet.” The FDA demanded immediate action, suggesting the online marketers cease and desist from using the language cited in the FDA’s warning letter from their online advertising. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
